<title>JAPAN: Japan MOF to auction 10-yr JGBs on Tuesday.</title>
<headline>Japan MOF to auction 10-yr JGBs on Tuesday.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Ministry of Finance (MOF) is planning to offer 10-year Japanese government bonds through a price-competitive auction on Tuesday, a MOF official said on Monday.</p>
<p>Bond traders said that judging from current market conditions, the coupon rate for the 10-year bonds is likely to be kept at a record low of 2.6 percent, unchanged from the latest 193rd 10-year JGBs.</p>
<p>The offer amount is also likely to be left unchanged at one trillion yen, a trader for a trust bank's securities unit said.</p>
<p>--Tokyo Treasury Desk, +81-3-5473-3748</p>
